.TH "DOCUMENT.SELECTIONCHANGE_EVENT" "3JS" "August 28, 2026" "JavaScript" "JavaScript Reference Manual"
.SH NAME
Document.selectionchange_event \- Document: selectionchange event
.SH SYNOPSIS
The browser fires the \f[B]\f[CB]selectionchange\f[B]\f[R] event of the
Selection API when the current \f[CR]Selection\f[R] of a
\f[CR]Document\f[R] changes.
A document selection represents either a range of selected content
across DOM nodes or a collapsed caret position.
.PP
This event is not cancelable and does not bubble.
.SH SYNTAX
Use the event name in methods like \f[CR]addEventListener()\f[R], or set
an event handler property.
.IP
.EX
addEventListener(\(dqselectionchange\(dq, (event) => {})

onselectionchange = (event) => {}
.EE
.SH EVENT TYPE
A generic \f[CR]Event\f[R].
.SH DESCRIPTION
The \f[CR]Document\f[R] object \f[CR]selectionchange\f[R] event is fired
when:
.IP \(bu 2
A user or script creates or clears a selection.
.IP \(bu 2
The start or end boundary point of a selected range moves.
.IP \(bu 2
A selected range changes completely.
.IP \(bu 2
A selection collapses to a single caret position.
.PP
The event object itself does not contain the updated selection details.
You can retrieve the current selection by calling
\f[CR]document.getSelection()\f[R] within your event listener.
.RS
.PP
\f[B]Note:\f[R] When you change the selection programmatically, for
example by calling \f[CR]Selection.collapse()\f[R], the selection
updates immediately, but the \f[CR]selectionchange\f[R] event is queued
as a task.
Its listeners run later, after the current script finishes executing.
This contrasts with events such as \f[CR]focus\f[R] and
\f[CR]click\f[R], whose listeners run synchronously when triggered by
\f[CR]focus()\f[R] and \f[CR]click()\f[R], respectively.
.RE
.PP
This event differs significantly from the \f[CR]selectionchange\f[R]
event fired on \f[CR]<input>\f[R] and \f[CR]<textarea>\f[R] text
controls:
.IP \(bu 2
Document selections use DOM node positions and require
\f[CR]Document.getSelection()\f[R] for inspection.
Text inputs maintain independent selections within their internal text
values, using character offsets inspected via \f[CR]selectionStart\f[R],
\f[CR]selectionEnd\f[R], and \f[CR]selectionDirection\f[R].
.IP \(bu 2
The document\-level \f[CR]selectionchange\f[R] event fires directly on
the \f[CR]Document\f[R] and does not bubble.
The text input \f[CR]selectionchange\f[R] event fires on the
input/textarea element and bubbles up the DOM tree.
.PP
See the \f[CR]selectionchange\f[R] event of \f[CR]HTMLInputElement\f[R]
and the \f[CR]selectionchange\f[R] event of
\f[CR]HTMLTextAreaElement\f[R] for more details of the text input
events.
.SH EXAMPLES
.SS Basic usage
.IP
.EX
\f[I]// addEventListener version\f[R]
document.addEventListener(\(dqselectionchange\(dq, () \f[B]=>\f[R] {
  console.log(document.getSelection());
});

\f[I]// onselectionchange version\f[R]
document.onselectionchange = () \f[B]=>\f[R] {
  console.log(document.getSelection());
};
.EE
.SH SEE ALSO
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]selectstart\f[R]
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]Document.getSelection()\f[R]
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]Selection\f[R]
